LN(1)                          User Commands                           LN(1)

NAME
    ln - give a file a second name

SYNOPSIS
    ln OLD NEW

DESCRIPTION
    Make NEW a hard link to the regular file OLD. Both names refer to one
    file: a write through either is seen through the other, and the data
    lasts until the last name is removed. NEW is created in the working
    directory.

    Only a regular file can be linked, and only within one directory:
    NEW goes beside a name the file already has. A link into another
    directory is refused (EXDEV), as a move is.

    Through a session's capability the file travels with the request as
    a capability, never as an inode number, and the new name may give no
    more than you already hold on the file: a file you may only read gets
    no writable second name in a writable directory. Without a session,
    you must own the file.

SEE ALSO
    rm(1), stat(1)
